  "boxes": [
    {
      "type": "anchorbox",
      "title": "The Bridge of Advocacy",
      "description": "In the *Valmiki Ramayana* (*Yuddha Kanda, 17:50-68*), when Vibhishana sought refuge, Sugriva and other leaders suspected him of being a spy. Hanuman was the sole advisor who delivered a brilliant, analytical speech to Lord Rama, advocating for Vibhishana's acceptance. Because Vibhishana was accepted and protected based on Hanuman's fair advocacy (this 'Mantra' or counsel to Rama), he was crowned King of Lanka (*Lankeshvara*). It shows how a true leader's strategic advocacy can lift others to greatness.",
      "motivating_text": "",
      "citation": ""
    }
  ]
